Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedbuzzertest.shoddy — test program for seedbuzzer.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the cuttletest / reckonertest / seedtest pattern:
Rem it prints what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion
Rem that fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem IT NEEDS NO SOUND CARD, and that is buzzer's own contract rather
Rem than a concession here: with no audio device every sound word is a
Rem NO-OP rather than a failure, so a tune queues identically on a
Rem machine that can play it and one that cannot. What the suite
Rem asserts is therefore everything except the noise — that a score
Rem parses to the right length, that every malformed one is refused
Rem naming the position, and that the queue bookkeeping is real.
Rem
Rem THE PARSER IS THE INTERESTING PART. buzzer.shoddy was rewritten to
Rem thread a Result so that TryMmlNotes could exist, and MmlNotes is now
Rem that answer with the Err turned back into an abort. So there are two
Rem things worth proving: that the guarded form reports each of the five
Rem malformed cases, and that the ABORTING form still behaves exactly as
Rem it did — which is what the machine's own C# suite covers, and what
Rem BUZZLENGTH below re-checks from this side by measuring known scores.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\seedbuzzertest.shoddy      (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/cuttle.shoddy"
Include "../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/str.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedbuzzer.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading an answer ------------------------------------------------

Def Ran(st As RckState, line As String) As RckState
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Def Bad(st As RckState, line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Why(st As RckState, line As String) As String
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            why
        Case Else
            ""

Def Text(st As RckState) As String
    Join(Map(CutCells(RckStack(st)), Fn(c) => CutShow(c, RckFmt(st))), " | ")

Def TopNum(st As RckState) As Number
    If CutDepth(RckStack(st)) < 1 Then
        0 - 999999
    Else
        NumOf(First(CutCells(RckStack(st))))

Def NumOf(c As Cell) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            x
        Case Else
            0 - 999999

Def Q(s As String) As String
    Chr(34) & s & Chr(34)

Rem Safe for every word here: nothing this seed does opens or closes
Rem anything, and re-queueing a tune three times is only more sound.
Rem The one exception is anything measured against the QUEUE, which is
Rem why those are run once and read.
Def Refuses(st As RckState, line As String, part As String) As Boolean
    Bad(st, line) And Instr(Why(st, line), part) > 0 And Text(Ran(st, line)) = Text(st) And Text(Ran(Ran(st, line), "1 1 +")) = Text(Ran(st, "1 1 +"))

Def Near(a As Number, b As Number) As Boolean
    Abs(a - b) <= 0.001

Def Main()
    Let s0 = RckSeedBuzzer(RckNew())
    Let g = Ran(s0, "1 2")

    Print("--- the seed is in the dictionary, grouped and documented ---")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "BUZZPLAY") And RckKnows(s0, "BUZZFREQ") And RckKnows(s0, "BUZZLENGTH"), "THE WORDS ARE THERE")
    Assert(Contains(RckWords(s0), "-- seed-buzzer --"), "AND THEY HAVE A GROUP OF THEIR OWN")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => WordEffect(e) <> "" And WordDesc(e) <> ""), "NO WORD IS WITHOUT AN EFFECT LINE AND A DESCRIPTION")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Length(RckHelp(s0, WordName(e))) = 3), "AND HELP ANSWERS FOR EVERY ONE OF THEM")
    Rem A sound is FIRED, not opened — there is no handle and no name to
    Rem bind, which is what makes this the odd one out among the seeds
    Rem that reach a device.
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Instr(Lower(WordEffect(e)), "handle") = 0), "NO WORD'S EFFECT STRING MENTIONS A HANDLE")
    Assert(Not RckKnows(s0, "BUZZOPEN") And Not RckKnows(s0, "BUZZCLOSE"), "AND THERE IS NO OPEN OR CLOSE — A SOUND IS FIRED, NOT HELD")
    Assert(IsEmpty(RckBoundNames(Ran(g, "1 " & Q("CDE") & " BUZZPLAY"))), "AND PLAYING BINDS NOTHING")

    Print("--- the pure half: a note's frequency, and a score's length ---")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("A4") & " BUZZFREQ")), 440), "A4 IS 440 HERTZ, WHICH IS THE ONE EVERYBODY KNOWS")
    Assert(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("A5") & " BUZZFREQ")) > TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("A4") & " BUZZFREQ")), "AND AN OCTAVE UP IS HIGHER")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("A5") & " BUZZFREQ")), 880), "EXACTLY TWICE AS HIGH, WHICH IS WHAT AN OCTAVE MEANS")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("c4") & " BUZZFREQ")), TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("C4") & " BUZZFREQ"))), "AND A NOTE NAME IS CASE-INSENSITIVE")
    Rem A whole note is 4 * 60000 / tempo ms, so at T120 a quarter note
    Rem is 500ms and four of them are two seconds. This is the check that
    Rem the rewritten parser still computes what it always did.
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("T120 CDEF") & " BUZZLENGTH")), 2000), "FOUR QUARTER NOTES AT T120 IS TWO SECONDS")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("T60 CDEF") & " BUZZLENGTH")), 4000), "AND AT HALF THE TEMPO, TWICE AS LONG")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("T120 L8 CDEF") & " BUZZLENGTH")), 1000), "AND AT EIGHTH NOTES, HALF AS LONG")
    Rem A dot is one and a half times, which the parser reads separately
    Rem from the length digits.
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("T120 C4.") & " BUZZLENGTH")), 750), "A DOTTED QUARTER IS HALF AS LONG AGAIN")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(s0, Q("") & " BUZZLENGTH")), 0), "AND AN EMPTY SCORE TAKES NO TIME AT ALL")

    Print("--- every way an MML string can be malformed, each named ---")
    Rem These five were Errors in the machine until buzzer.shoddy was
    Rem rewritten to thread a Result. Each reports what is wrong AND
    Rem where, which is what makes a long score fixable.
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("CDEZ") & " BUZZPLAY", "UNEXPECTED 'Z' AT POSITION 4"), "AN UNKNOWN COMMAND, NAMING THE CHARACTER AND THE POSITION")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("O9 C") & " BUZZPLAY", "OCTAVE OUT OF RANGE 0-8"), "AN OCTAVE PAST THE TOP")
    Rem The default octave is 4, so it takes five steps down to fall off
    Rem the bottom — and the fifth is the one that must be caught, not
    Rem the first.
    Assert(Not Bad(g, "1 " & Q("<<<< C") & " BUZZPLAY"), "FOUR STEPS DOWN FROM THE DEFAULT REACHES OCTAVE 0, WHICH IS FINE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("<<<<< C") & " BUZZPLAY", "OCTAVE OUT OF RANGE 0-8"), "AND THE FIFTH FALLS OFF THE BOTTOM")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("T C") & " BUZZPLAY", "T NEEDS A NUMBER"), "A TEMPO WITH NO NUMBER AFTER IT")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("T0 C") & " BUZZPLAY", "T MUST BE AT LEAST 1"), "AND A TEMPO OF NOTHING")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("C0") & " BUZZPLAY", "BAD LENGTH"), "A NOTE LENGTH OF ZERO")
    Rem The same five reach BUZZLENGTH, which parses and plays nothing —
    Rem so a score can be checked without being committed to a channel.
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q("CDEZ") & " BUZZLENGTH", "UNEXPECTED 'Z'"), "AND BUZZLENGTH REFUSES THEM TOO, WITHOUT QUEUEING A NOTE")

    Print("--- a bad note name, which was the other abort ---")
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q("H4") & " BUZZFREQ", "BAD NOTE NAME 'H4'"), "A LETTER THAT IS NOT A NOTE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q("C") & " BUZZFREQ", "BAD NOTE NAME"), "A NAME WITH NO OCTAVE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q("C9") & " BUZZFREQ", "BAD NOTE NAME"), "AN OCTAVE PAST THE TOP")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("H4") & " 250 BUZZNOTE", "BAD NOTE NAME"), "AND BUZZNOTE REFUSES THE SAME")

    Print("--- the channel, the loudness and the waveform ---")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "9 " & Q("C") & " BUZZPLAY", "FROM 1 TO 8"), "A CHANNEL PAST THE LAST")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "0 " & Q("C") & " BUZZPLAY", "FROM 1 TO 8"), "AND CHANNEL ZERO")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1.5 " & Q("C") & " BUZZPLAY", "BUZZPLAY"), "AND A FRACTIONAL ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 2 BUZZGAIN", "LOUDNESS RUNS FROM 0 TO 1"), "A LOUDNESS ABOVE ONE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 -1 BUZZGAIN", "LOUDNESS RUNS FROM 0 TO 1"), "AND BELOW ZERO")
    Assert(Not Bad(g, "1 0 BUZZGAIN"), "BUT SILENCE IS A LOUDNESS")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 " & Q("wobble") & " BUZZWAVE", "IS NOT A WAVEFORM"), "A WAVEFORM THAT IS NOT ONE, LISTING THE THREE THAT ARE")
    Assert(Not Bad(g, "1 " & Q("SINE") & " BUZZWAVE"), "AND A WAVEFORM NAME IS CASE-INSENSITIVE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 -100 250 BUZZTONE", "FREQUENCY CANNOT BE NEGATIVE"), "A NEGATIVE FREQUENCY")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "1 440 -5 BUZZTONE", "LESS THAN NO TIME"), "AND A NEGATIVE DURATION")
    Assert(Not Bad(g, "1 0 250 BUZZTONE"), "BUT A FREQUENCY OF 0 IS A REST, WHICH IS ORDINARY")

    Print("--- the queue, which is the fault nothing could see coming ---")
    Rem SOUNDQUEUE refuses more than five minutes queued ahead, and until
    Rem SOUNDQUEUED there was no way to ask what was already in front of
    Rem you. Run ONCE and read, because unlike everything above these
    Rem really do change the channel.
    Let q0 = Ran(g, "8 BUZZSTOP")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(q0, "8 BUZZQUEUED")), 0), "A CHANNEL JUST STOPPED HAS NOTHING QUEUED")
    Let q1 = Ran(q0, "8 " & Q("T120 CDEF") & " BUZZPLAY")
    Assert(TopNum(Ran(q1, "8 BUZZQUEUED")) > 1000, "AND AFTER A TWO-SECOND TUNE IT HAS SECONDS IN FRONT OF IT")
    Assert(TopNum(Ran(q1, "8 BUZZQUEUED")) <= 2000, "AND NO MORE THAN THE TUNE WAS LONG")
    Rem A score longer than the cap is refused whole, before a note of it
    Rem is queued — a tune half queued is a tune that has already started.
    Assert(Refuses(q1, "8 " & Q("T1 L1 CCCCCCCCCC CCCCCCCCCC CCCCCCCCCC") & " BUZZPLAY", "MORE THAN 5 MINUTES AHEAD"), "A SCORE LONGER THAN THE CAP, NAMING THE CHANNEL AND THE REMEDY")
    Assert(TopNum(Ran(q1, "8 BUZZQUEUED")) <= 2000, "AND THAT REFUSAL QUEUED NOTHING")
    Let q2 = Ran(q1, "8 BUZZSTOP")
    Assert(Near(TopNum(Ran(q2, "8 BUZZQUEUED")), 0), "AND BUZZSTOP THROWS AWAY WHAT WAS WAITING")

    Print("--- and the session is exactly as it was ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(g, "1 1 +")) = "2 | 2 | 1", "THE STACK IS STILL THERE AND STILL EVALUATING")

    Print("")
    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
